  "hotelDescription": "With St Paul\u0027s Cathedral to one side, Tate Modern to the other, and the City on your doorstep, it\u0027s hard to get more central than Premier Inn London Blackfriars. \n\nIn fact, for a short break, we\u0027re perfectly placed. Wander to the West End and Covent Garden. Stroll along the Thames to Big Ben and the London Eye. Or catch a show at the world- famous Mermaid Theatre, just next door. And, with many of the world\u0027s biggest companies just minutes away, we\u0027re ideal for business trips too. Whether it\u0027s been work or play, you\u0027ll return to a friendly team, extra-comfy beds and an excellent breakfast.",
  "hotelDirections": "From Blackfriars train station (Mainline and Circle/District Tube lines) - cross over New Bridge Street (A201) and turn left into Tudor Street. The hotel is 50 metres on the right hand side on Dorset Rise. By car - the hotel is located just off the A201 and is within the congestion zone. There is no car parking at the hotel.",
